From 084664152d9126a62b0cfe2c7f3d5bc0859608a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 21:58:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 9 plan 09-02b mojom + ExportService

Lands the Profile-decoupled half of the export pipeline so the
Settings WebUI work can be approached separately.

- chrome/browser/phlink/portability/portability.mojom: ExportStatus
  enum, ProgressObserver interface, Exporter interface
  (ObserveProgress + Export). Lives in the phlink.portability.mojom
  module.
- export_service.{h,cc}: ExportProfileToBundle(profile_dir, dest_path,
  passphrase) and an include-list-overridable variant for tests.
  Skips missing profile files (Chromium does not always create every
  file in every profile until first use). Returns ExportStatus
  mirroring the mojom enum.
- export_service_unittest.cc: empty-passphrase rejection +
  end-to-end round-trip from a hand-built temp profile dir through
  BundleWriter and back through BundleReader.

The Settings WebUI Export card (Lit element + chrome://settings/portability
route + localized strings) is the remaining piece and lands in a
follow-up patch (slot 0122).
